/**
\page tolink_lane iccApplyToLink: sampled DeviceLink and Cube lane

\tableofcontents

\section tolink_contract Positional argv contract

This tool has one direct positional form:

`iccApplyToLink dst_link link_type lut_size option title range_min range_max first_transform interp profile intent ...`

The first ten process tokens include the executable and the nine fixed fields.
Every remaining token belongs to profile/intent pairs, with `-ENV:sig value`
and `-PCC file` participating in that pair-shaped sequence. An odd remainder
is rejected before a writer or CMM is created.

\dotfile tolink-lane.dot "iccApplyToLink validation, CMM sampling, and writer lane"

\section tolink_options Fixed fields

| Position | Allowed value | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `dst_link` | output path | ICC DeviceLink profile or text Cube LUT to create. |
| `link_type` | 0, 1 | DeviceLink or `.cube` text file. |
| `lut_size` | integer 2 through 255 | Grid entries along each source dimension. |
| `option`, DeviceLink | 0, 1 | ICC V4 16-bit table or V5 profile. |
| `option`, Cube | integer 0 through 20 | Decimal precision for Cube entries. |
| `title` | text | Output description. |
| `range_min`, `range_max` | finite floats, min less than max | Input domain sampled by every grid axis. |
| `first_transform` | 0, 1 | Destination or source transform from the first profile. |
| `interp` | 0, 1 | Linear or tetrahedral interpolation. |

The range is not an output clipping range. Node zero samples `range_min` and
the final node samples `range_max`. A non-default range requires V5 or Cube:
V4 DeviceLinks cannot declare that altered input domain.

\section tolink_runtime Sampling and safety gates

The tool parses every fixed field before building the CMM. It adds profiles to
`CIccCmm`, applies environment and PCC controls, and calls `Begin()`. After
the CMM supplies source/destination spaces and channel counts,
`IccLinkGridFits()` proves both node count and node-count-times-destination
channels fit the CLUT representation. Only then does the selected writer
allocate a CLUT.

The generation loop walks the n-dimensional grid, maps each index to the
validated input range, calls `CIccCmm::Apply()`, and sends the destination
pixel to either `CDevLinkWriter` or `CCubeWriter`.

\section tolink_qa QA example

`iccApplyToLink-quick-check.sh` checks DeviceLink and Cube output plus type,
LUT-size, range, option, transform, and interpolation rejection boundaries.
*/
